## 5. The Golden Rule as Ethical Invariant

### 5.1 Universal Ethics

Fractal Binary, as implemented in SCOS, is not ethically neutral. It prescribes the Golden Rule as the universal ethical invariant against which all claims are validated. This is not a subjective preference but a formal requirement:

> **The Golden Rule Theorem (GRT):** Any claim that violates the Golden Rule cannot be added to the chain, regardless of its logical consistency.

This theorem is grounded in the recognition that ethics is prior to logic. Logic is a tool; ethics is the practice that guides its use.

### 5.2 W7 and the Unwitnessed

The Golden Rule is extended through W7 to include future generations, unseen perspectives, and the truth itself. This ensures that the system is not merely a consensus of the powerful but a consensus of the just. W7 is the fractal recursion of ethics, holding the system accountable to those who cannot yet speak.

